 the bill does:** Section 220.5(a) forbids schools and boards to \"enact or enforce any policy, rule, or administrative regulation that would require an employee or a contractor to disclose\" a pupil's gender identity without the pupil's consent. That is the rung-2 clause, so I coded it `chair-shaped`.\n- **Why not rung 1:** the bill forbids rules that require disclosure. It does not require staff to keep the information from parents.\n- **Why not rungs 3–5:** any school rule requiring staff to tell parents, on request or by notice, is exactly the kind of rule the bill forbids.\n- **Why it isn't preemption:** the codebook's preemption rule makes such a law `adjacent`, but it carves out rungs that are themselves about forbidding another level's rules. Rung 2 is one, so the passage is `on-question`.\n- **Vote and text match:** the chaptered text is the Senate amendment of 2024-05-22, which is the text the Senate voted on.\n- **Evidence and gaps:** `rests_on` holds both passages of the one vote. The vote page carries the name and tally quotes; the bill-text page carries the provision quote. Code will compute the tier as `single-source`. The sources contain no words of his own, so `quotes` and `needs_source` are both empty.","ttft_ms":13880,"type":"result","duration_ms":31937,"uuid":"0797a0e3-93be-4b9b-82cd-1828a817cc19","ttft_stream_ms":2401,"time_to_request_ms":710,"first_content_frame_ms":2402,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
